  "theorem": "Every rank-m conservative Schur mediator induces a positive semidefinite matrix of rank at most m. Eckart--Young--Mirsky proves that the best rank-m approximation to gA retains its m largest eigenmodes. The exact Frobenius error is the Euclidean norm of the discarded eigenvalues and the exact operator error is the largest discarded eigenvalue. Thus lower-rank mediators source selected stiff modes, not the full strict geometry."
